  "categories_thin": [
    "Land surveying - one New Brunswick-based firm (Professional Land Services); most surveyors covering the city are based in Piscataway or Flemington.",
    "Real estate appraisal - one local firm (Thompson Appraisal Service); most appraisers serving the city are in Edison/Franklin.",
    "Title agencies - two New Brunswick addresses only; several 'New Brunswick title company' web pages belong to agencies based elsewhere and were excluded.",
    "Environmental consulting - only Aguilar Environmental is New Brunswick-based; TRC is a national firm with a local office.",
    "Financial advisory - difficult to separate real New Brunswick offices from advisors at virtual/registered addresses on George St; TIAA and J.P. Morgan/Chase branches were excluded as large institutions.",
    "Legal - extremely dense (60+ small firms and sole practitioners); more almost certainly exist inside the 303/317 George St, 46 Bayard St and 40 Paterson St suites that no public directory fully indexes."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Zone check: all of New Brunswick NJ sits roughly 4-5 miles straight-line from central Milltown (40.4498,-74.4407), so the entire town is inside the 10-mile radius; no part of the zone falls outside it.",
    "317 George St (especially Suite 320 and Suite 412) and 100/120 Albany St are multi-tenant or virtual-office buildings; several listed firms, national-firm satellites and out-of-town consultancies may be registered rather than staffed there.",
    "Excluded as chains/large institutions even though present in New Brunswick: CBIZ, CGI, TIAA, J.P. Morgan Wealth Management at Chase, Morgan Stanley/Smith Barney office, Spherion and PeopleReady (staffing chains/franchises), State Farm agent office, Coldwell Banker and RE/MAX franchise offices, and Central Jersey Legal Services (nonprofit legal aid).",
    "Slalom, TRC, Windels Marx and Brach Eichler are larger firms with a New Brunswick presence; kept in but flagged because size at the site is unverified.",
    "Many entries come from a single bulk directory (Yellow Pages/Superpages/Cylex/AllPages/LoopNet/FindOpen/firmania/loc8nearme) and were not confirmed on an own website; active_evidence marks these.",
    "Only published business contact details were collected - no personal names, home addresses or personal phone numbers."
  ],
  "data_gaps": [
    "BBB, Yellow Pages, Superpages, Manta, Cylex, ChamberofCommerce.com, FindOpen, AllPages and Cornell LII returned HTTP 403 to direct fetching; Yellow Pages also blocked in-browser with a Cloudflare challenge. Their data was used only through search-result summaries.",
    "Overpass API mirrors timed out on large office=* / shop=estate_agent queries for the New Brunswick bounding box; only a small office=lawyer set was retrieved, so OSM coverage is incomplete (the primary Overpass endpoint was unreachable from this machine).",
    "The shared browser session was switched between agents mid-run, interrupting planned Bing Maps category sweeps (insurance, financial advisors, property management, architecture, IT). Those categories were covered through searches instead, so small map-only operators may be missing.",
    "Attorney Daniel Santarsiero (53 Paterson St) is flagged 'temporarily closed' on maps and was not listed; Karina Lucid/Lucid Law lists its New Brunswick office as temporarily closed with the active office in Bridgewater, so it was excluded.",
    "Kanika Malhotra (111 Livingston Ave, 732-247-3600) appears to be an attorney at RAM Law and was merged into that entry rather than listed separately.",
    "Addresses could not be verified for Penn Properties Management, New Brunswick Property Management LLC, Bussel Realty Corp, VensIT Corp, The Harrison Group, Yonta Law, Ginarte's New Brunswick office and Cintron Firm.",
    "The city's shop-local listing site (newbrunswick.com) is fetchable per business but its category index URL could not be located, so it was not mined in bulk."
  ]
